WEBVTT

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.910
Listen up, my friends!

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:07.250
We're going to take photos of stars for
the September contest now!

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.450
Okay.
Yeah!
'Kay.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:12.410
Treat the rental SLR cameras and camera gear with care!

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:13.120
Okay!

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.830
Hajime-chan, how many times was that?

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:17.750
When I say "stars," I mean nudes!

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.700
I see. That is profound.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.040
No, Charles, Pin-senpai is all about nudes.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.120
I can see them even if I close my eyes! I can see them!

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:33.370
I can vividly, intensely, and furiously see the female body
that shines in the night sky with my mind's eye.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.160
I can't see anything!

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.370
Yeah, I can see them.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:42.200
Hey, Charles! Open your eyes!
We're going to end up becoming stars!

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.120
What?!

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:50.950
Wow! I've always wanted to see Mount Fuji! It's so big!

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.500
Unfortunately, it's shrouded by clouds.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:54.120
Yeah.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:59.370
These are our plans for later, but we're going to check in
to the inn, take a short break, have supper...

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.000
Time                    Itinerary
2018 Photography Club Training Camp Goal
Theme: "Stars" (Aim for the contest grand prize!!)

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.080
...then we're going to take pictures
from midnight until sunrise.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.040
Okay!

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.540
But will we be able to see the stars?

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:09.370
The weather forecaster said it'll be clear skies
at night, right, Mitsuyoshi?

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.410
Yeah.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.290
Uh...

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.290
Did you say you were a rain-bringer?

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:18.790
Are you serious?! Teresa-chan brought the rain?!

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.120
I did...?

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:22.450
I'm kidding.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.120
Wait, that was a joke?!

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.500
Then, let's go pray for the skies to clear!

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.660
Let's do it.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.540
Roger!
Indeed.
Okay!

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:40.660
Tada Never Falls in Love

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.080
Chotto matte kocchi muite
Hey, look over here

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.500
Finder wa itsumo kimatte
The viewfinder is always set

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.910
Kimi ja nai to pin to konai
If it isn't of you, then it doesn't appeal to me

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:54.080
Boku wa douka shichatta no kai?
Did something happen to me?

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:57.410
"O-tomodachi" o toorikoshite
I walked past my friends

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.540
Surechigai no koibito-miman mo
And my close friend, whom I keep missing

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:03.040
Sore wa souzoushii sekai
It's a turbulent world

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:07.410
Ki ga tsukeba, marude niji no you sa
By the time I realized it, the world was like a rainbow

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:10.830
Kisetsu yo tomare
Oh, seasons, stop

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:16.910
Kimi to kiritotta jikan ga, shashin no naka de
In the photos of our time together

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:22.290
Are mo kore mo sore mo dore mo kagayaiten da yo
Every single thing is shining brightly

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:28.410
Nee kimi ni, kimi ni hitotsu tsutaetokitain da
Hey, there's one thing I want to tell you

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:35.500
Mou tomaranai, kakushi kirenai, omoi ga koko ni an da yo
I can't stop it or hide it anymore; that feeling is right here

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:43.750
Baby, omoide to iu film no naka e kimi ga tokete shimau mae ni
Baby, before you vanish into this film we call "memories"

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:48.500
Todoketai kotoba ga an da yo
There's something I want to tell you

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:54.250
"Ima kimi ni koi shiteru yo"
"I'm in love with you now"

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.000
Did You Say You Were a Rain-bringer?

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:04.580
Mt. Mikuni
#1

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.830
Wow! If I'm not mistaken, this was...

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.080
Did it stop raining in your heart?

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.160
Yes.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.410
Always make your heart...

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.790
...rainbow!

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:21.450
This was the place that appeared in
episode three of Rainbow Shogun season two!

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:23.370
Isn't that great, Teresa?

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.080
Yes!

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:33.330
Alec!

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.330
You're wide open!

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:38.000
I took your picture! I took your picture!

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.330
Speed it up, guys!

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.700
I took your picture, Alec! Alec!

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.410
'Kay!

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:49.080
FORTUNES
100 yen

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.120
It's been a long time since we got
our fortunes, huh, Mitsuyoshi?!

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:50.290
Yeah.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:54.620
Okay!

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.330
FORTUNE

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.120
This is it.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.910
They say you can draw your fortune
however many times you want.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.910
Wow! I got "excellent luck"!

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:03.250
Excellent Luck      Fortune

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:05.750
What does "Machibito onshin nashi kuru" mean?

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:09.080
It means the person you are waiting for will come.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.830
Huh? Doesn't that mean Teresa-chan
will get a boyfriend?!

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:15.830
I've heard that "machibito" doesn't necessarily
mean a significant other, though.

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:16.790
Really?

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:21.620
It might be a soulmate, but you could be captivated
with someone who will positively change your life.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:22.790
Huh...

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.120
Is that so?

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:24.660
What about you, Alec?

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.120
What did you get?
"The person you are waiting for will not come."

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.580
Considerable Luck           Fortune
Love: give up
The person you are waiting for: will not come

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.620
"Give up on love"?

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.830
Ugh! I got the same one as Alec-san!

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.910
Don't let it get to you!

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:37.620
What about you, Charles?

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:41.500
I got "good luck." It says that my luck with love is good.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.500
Oh, nice!

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:48.540
Yeah. They say that life without love
is the same as being dead.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:54.410
That means you're always in love, Charles.
You and I are the same.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.580
Life without HINA is the same as being dead!

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:03.500
Hajime-chan, everyone went to the observation deck.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.290
I thought God was backing me up.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:16.330
Don't be so depressed! It's just a fortune!
I drew "excellent luck" on my third try!

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:16.910
Huh?

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:21.330
It said that my luck with love would be the best!
Come with me to draw another fortune!

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:22.750
Right, Mitsuyoshi?

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:29.540
Yeah. I got "bad luck," but if this is the absolute
worst luck I have, it isn't so bad.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.750
That's great, Tada-senpai! You're super cool!

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:34.200
That cheered me up!

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.160
What?!

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.410
Hey, you two, come with me to draw another fortune!

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:42.160
It's important to have enthusiasm that's like,
"Love, come to me! Bring it on!"

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.250
What is love?

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:53.660
Love. That is everyone falling in love with me
in the way that I love myself!

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.330
Alec, don't hold back.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:01.830
You can fall madly in love with me! Come on, baby!

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.580
Please save your sleep-talking for when you're asleep!

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:03.450
Huh?

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:09.000
Love is indeed a complicated thing.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.580
Did you give up or something, Pin-senpai?

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:16.160
There is also love that sparks for the first time
once you know someone likes you.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:21.870
So, HINA has been head over heels
for me ever since that day.

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:25.450
Pin-senpai seriously has a blissful personality, huh?

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:29.080
Tada-senpai, what do you think?

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.830
Love, huh?

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:33.700
Mitsuyoshi?

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.580
Hey, that's so vague!

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:44.000
How do people fall in love with others?

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.160
They look at others' faces, don't they?

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:47.250
Faces?

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:52.250
Even the structure of the human brain
is extremely sensitive to faces.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.580
I see!

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:58.120
But only Pin-senpai would be sensitive to breasts.

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:00.790
You're absolutely right.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:03.330
BATH
Men's Bath

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:06.830
We feel so refreshed, huh, Yamashita Dog?

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:07.870
Yeah.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:09.200
That was a nice bath, huh?

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:09.910
Yeah.

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:11.250
Where is Sugimoto-kun?

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.700
I think he'll be out soon.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:16.000
I can see them! I can see them!

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:20.830
Oh, ping pong! Play with me,
Forever Alone Yamashita Dog!

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:21.540
What?

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:24.620
Just play with me, Forever Alone Yamashita Dog!

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:27.700
Ugh... Being forever alone has
nothing to do with ping pong!

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:29.910
Tada-kun... care to play a game?

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:30.830
What?! Come on, Forever Alone Yamashita Dog!

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:30.830
Sure.

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:41.410
Huh?

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.450
Good luck, Senpai!

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:44.290
What's the score?

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:47.500
Ijuin-kun just beat Yamashita-kun.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.620
Good game.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:03.540
Yeah!

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:07.040
Hey, Mitsuyoshi was annihilated!

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:12.040
Relax a little before nighttime.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.160
Okay.
Okay!
'Kay!

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:24.290
Okay. I understand.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:27.950
I'll give you an answer right after
I check my texts. I'll talk to you later.

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:32.000
Can't sleep, Alec?

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.910
The wind was bothering me. Pardon me.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:39.540
You don't have to be so obvious in running away.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:41.700
I wasn't trying to...

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:47.830
I say that, but I guess I'm the one who wants to run away.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:52.700
This was a long-awaited trip for me,
but work wound up following me here.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.540
If you'd like, here.

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:13.410
If you listen to this, you'll be able to shut out
the sound of the wind.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:21.200
Teresa, I'm going to buy water. Would you like some?

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.580
Yes, thank you.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:37.040
The rain has lifted! Let's go take pictures, my friends!

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:37.870
Okay!

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:39.540
Be careful out there!

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:40.870
Okay!

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:45.410
Having work when you've come all
the way out here has seriously gotta suck.

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:46.290
Yeah.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:49.660
Still, this is so heavy.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:51.870
This is seriously torture!

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:55.540
Your suffering will make the things ahead
that much more enjoyable. Right, Tada?

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:56.700
Yeah.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.540
Well, I can only do this sort of activity
with you until the end of this year.

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:04.250
Yeah, you're gonna be in college
next year, huh, Pin-senpai?

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.660
Did you say that Kyoto University was your first choice?

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:07.700
Indeed.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.620
Kyoto has a lot of shrines, right?

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:14.200
Yes, it’s a very lovely place.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.580
Kyoto is hot at this time of year.

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:22.410
Note: Kawadoko is a platform built over a river to alleviate the summer
heat and can be found at a few Kyoto restaurants.
Gozan no Okuribi is a Buddhist festival held in Kyoto on August 16.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:20.290
The kawadoko and Gozan no Okuribi
are pretty nice, you know.

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:22.450
Wow! That sounds like fun!

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:26.790
Well, fall, winter, and spring all have their own merits.

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:30.080
If I live over there next year, I'll show you around.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:33.700
Next year, huh?

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:40.540
Oh, yeah... Teresa-chan and Alec
won't be here next year, huh?

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:41.700
Yes, we won't.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.910
That makes me kinda sad...

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:45.250
Sure does...

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:51.160
Our study abroad had been set
for one year from the very beginning.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:54.620
Everything has a beginning and end. That's life.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:58.040
You say that, but you're actually sad, aren't you, Alec?

00:10:58.040 --> 00:10:58.750
Not particularly.

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:00.000
There you go again!

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:02.830
I got the message, so...

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.830
Can I silence you for real?

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:06.750
Eeek!

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.750
I'm gonna go save us a spot!

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.700
Well, I feel just a little sad.

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:16.120
Let's go, too!

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.000
Okay.

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:27.330
Whoa, we've got this place all to ourselves!

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.580
It's cloudy, after all.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.660
But there's some wind.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:31.700
That's true.

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:36.410
Okay, everyone, set your cameras in any position
you'd like, within speaking range.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.080
We're on standby until the stars appear!

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.160
Okay.
Roger that!
'Kay!

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:44.410
Let me see that.

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:46.830
There you go.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:47.660
I sincerely appreciate it!

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:50.950
You've got it on backwards.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:54.120
Thank you very much.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:56.620
Are you okay with this, Ijuin?

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:57.620
Thank you!

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:00.580
Just as you'd expect, the friend
you've gotta have around is Mitsuyoshi!

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:02.950
Hey, future super photographer!

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:03.830
You're being loud.

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:09.750
Tada-kun, did you always want to be
a photographer ever since you were little?

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.250
Huh? Yeah...

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:16.200
It's amazing that you've kept on
working towards the same dream!

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:20.620
Well, Teresa-chan, what do you want to be in the future?

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:21.500
Huh?

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:27.000
By the way, I wanna be an Iron Chef and a cook
that'll put everyone to shame! Wait, you knew that?!

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:34.870
I wanted to be a ballet dancer a long time ago.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:40.290
Oh, I know! I can totally imagine you
as a ballerina, Teresa-chan!

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.250
You can definitely be one! Uh-huh, uh-huh!

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:46.870
I'd be happy if I could. But I didn't grow any taller,
so I couldn't become one.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:48.620
What?! So, you quit?!

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:49.410
Yes!

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:52.160
Then, what about now? What do you want to be?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.580
Nothing worth mentioning right now...

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:55.330
Huh?

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.250
I want to live life with a smile on my face, if I can.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:02.250
What?! That's all you dream of?!
Wait, are you okay with that, Teresa-chan?

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:03.750
That's no good!

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:05.870
Be ambitious, girl!

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:12.290
She's fine. People who always smile
are perfect in mind and body.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.200
Huh?

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:20.580
I read somewhere in a book that said one thing Gagarin
the cosmonaut was chosen for was his big smile.

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:22.410
Thank you.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:28.750
I'm going to pour some coffee.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.040
Okay!

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:32.620
I made it strong.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:34.040
It's good!

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:34.750
Yeah!

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.750
Like I said, the friend you've gotta
have around is Mitsuyoshi!

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:38.450
Yeah!

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:41.160
Now, staying up all night is no big deal!

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:46.750
What did he mean when he said, "no big deal"?

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:47.750
Who knows?

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.660
He's a happy person, huh?

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:07.160
Please have some water, if you'd like.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:08.290
I sincerely appreciate it.

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:10.120
You sincerely appreciate it?

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.700
We can't see the stars, huh?

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:25.870
One more step, and you would've been in the lake.

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:29.410
Oh... I-I sincerely appreciate it.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:34.830
I think the stars will come into view soon,
once these clouds drift away for us.

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:37.120
Yeah.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:38.580
Mitsuyoshi!

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:42.250
A chicken rode on a gorilla and flew in the sky!

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:45.700
The gorilla...

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:45.700
He's just sleep-talking!

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:59.000
Were you awake this entire time, Tada-kun?

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:03.500
I took a nap earlier at the inn, because
this kind of opportunity is hard to come by.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.660
And I want to take a nice picture.

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:08.250
Why do you work so hard?

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:10.660
Am I?

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:20.870
Yes. Ever since I first met you, you were always
taking pictures or helping out at the coffee shop!

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:22.620
I go to school, too, you know.

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:24.500
That's true.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:30.500
But I just felt that you truly do the best
that you can all the time.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.080
After our dad and mom passed away,

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:51.370
I somehow might've kept thinking
that I needed to grow up quickly.

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:57.250
Huh?!

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:04.160
Did anything happen to you
a long time ago, too, Teresa?

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:07.370
Why?

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:11.330
When you saw my dad's last photo, you said:

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:17.580
I bet you've been living your life wishing
to be stronger ever since that day.

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:26.000
At that time, I was like, "Yeah, she's right.
How does she know that?"

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:29.660
I wondered if you were talking about yourself.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.000
Well...

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:47.290
Yes, I may have realized that I needed to grow up
quickly when I was seven years old, too.

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:53.330
Miss Teresa!

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:54.450
Huh?

00:16:56.500 --> 00:17:03.040
Please be more considerate of
your situation... before acting!

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.700
Alec...

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:14.580
I realized for the first time that my actions hurt someone.

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:16.910
It hurt someone?

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:24.080
I made someone, who's very dear to me, cry.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:29.660
I felt really sad and apologetic.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:34.000
I would want to go back to that time,
if it were possible.

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:43.040
It'd be nice if you could, but you can't.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:52.830
You should just try not to repeat
the same mistakes, shouldn't you?

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:59.910
I think that's what it means to regret.

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:10.790
Well, I don't mean to talk so big.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.080
The stars are out!

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:31.950
Wow! They're so pretty!

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:34.200
That's the Milky Way!

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:40.410
It's caught between the Summer Triangle's
Vega, Altair, and Deneb.

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:41.330
Yeah!

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:46.950
And that's the North Star.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:48.120
Yeah...

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:53.290
It's a lucky sign that always shows us the way.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:08.040
Mitsuyoshi!

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:12.830
Huh? What, what, what, what?!
What's wrong, Teresa-chan?!

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:13.660
Uh...

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:15.910
I-I'm sorry!

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:19.250
It's 'cause you startled her! Right?

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:20.700
Y-yeah...

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.620
Really? I'm sorry.

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:25.660
Wait! There are so many stars out!

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:26.950
Yeah.

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:30.790
Wow! Stars, everyone! Wake up, wake up!

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:36.870
Whoa! Pin-senpai, stars!

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:40.040
They're out, huh?

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:41.700
Hey, Class Rep.

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:44.620
Hinako.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:45.540
Huh?

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.790
Wow! The skies have cleared!

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.330
All right! Let's take some pictures!

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:51.370
'Kay!

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:52.660
Okay!

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:15.330
Wow! It's so pretty!

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:32.250
I had a fun summer break, thanks to you, Teresa.

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:36.750
If anything comes up, call me right away.

00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:38.370
Okay.

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:44.080
TAKOYAKI

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:41.330
Takoyaki!

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:42.410
You're right.

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:44.120
Wait here.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:54.370
Alec, have a little more faith in Teresa.

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:56.790
This is the last time, after all.

00:20:57.410 --> 00:21:03.370
Neither Teresa nor I can live venturing off
our paths that easily.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:04.870
I sincerely appreciate it!

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:08.370
Sir Charles...

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:11.500
Charles, here's a souvenir!

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:12.950
Thank you.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:20.290
Well, Princess Teresa,
I'll be waiting for you in Larsenburg.

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:22.290
Okay.

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:25.950
I'll be waiting for you, too, Alec.
Take care of Teresa for me.

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:27.540
Understood.

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:38.790
I love you just the way you are.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:48.080
There's something I'd like to talk
to you about, Miss Teresa.

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:48.790
Huh?

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:12.660
Itsumademo tsuzuite yuku to, boku wa zutto omottetan da yo
I kept wondering how long this would last

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:23.910
Ano hi kimi ga kirei sugiru wake o, boku wa nani mo shiranakatta
I had no idea why you were so pretty that day

00:22:24.830 --> 00:22:30.160
Kamisama tte hito ga kimi o tsuresatte
After taking you away, someone who calls himself "God"

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:36.120
Ni-do to wa aenai to boku ni iu
Says that I will never see you again

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:41.750
Doko ni ikun da yo, boku wa nani mo dekinakatta yo
Where are you going? There was nothing I could do

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:46.750
Utsukushi sugita hito yo
You beautiful person

00:22:47.700 --> 00:22:53.250
Aitakute, aitakute donna kimi demo
I miss you so much

00:22:53.500 --> 00:22:58.870
Negaigoto ga moshi hitotsu kanau naraba
If one of my wishes were to come true

00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:04.830
Imasugu ni, imasugu ni dakishimetain da yo
I would want to hold you tight right now

00:23:04.830 --> 00:23:10.450
Zutto kimi no soba ni dake itakattan da
I only wanted to be with you forever

00:23:10.750 --> 00:23:15.620
Kokoro no naka wa namida no ame no melody
Within my heart is a melody of a flood of tears

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:24.330
Kimi to sugoshita hibi wa wasureru nante dekinain da yo
I can't ever forget the days I spent with you

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:29.830
I had a fun summer break,
thanks to you and your friends, Tada-kun.

00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:30.700
I'm glad.

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:33.250
The peaches I bought on my trip sure were tasty.

00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:34.830
I meant to share them, but...

00:23:35.290 --> 00:23:38.500
Next time: Episode 9, "I Don't Have One Now."

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:41.040
I Don't Have One Now

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:39.580
That's too bad.

00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:40.830
Until next time, everyone!
